\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every pure type system with arbitrary sorts, axioms and rules, if every legal expression in every valid context has some terminating $\beta$-reduction sequence, must every $\beta$-reduction sequence of each such expression terminate? Reduction includes type annotations and the specification need not be functional.

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every pure type system with arbitrary sorts, axioms and rules, if every legal expression in every valid context has some terminating $\beta$-reduction sequence, must every $\beta$-reduction sequence of each such expression terminate? Reduction includes type annotations and the specification need not be functional.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2023/6}.
\item[S2] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Weak-and-strong-normalization-in-pure-type-systems-September-25-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

